# PoC run 2 (-memory old): load the secret y stored in run 1, multiply by
# an attacker-chosen x, and reveal.
#
# Between runs the attacker (Player 1) incremented its MAC-key share alpha_1
# (so the global key is now alpha+1) and -- for the full input-guessing
# variant -- added a guess g to its share of y's MAC tag.  The Beaver triple
# consumed by the multiply is fresh under alpha+1, so the mask-opening MAC
# check passes iff the (zero-check or guess) condition on y holds.
#
# Player 1 enters x = 0, so the revealed output is always 0 and leaks nothing
# about y; the protocol abort (or not) is the side channel.
y = sint.load_mem(100)
print_ln("Player 1, please enter x (use 0 for clean selective failure):")
x = sint.get_private_input_from(1)
z = x * y
print_ln("z = %s", z.reveal())
